description.narrative:
The overall goal of the CMDTF is to foster the establishment of efficient capital markets in Africa that can effectively mobilize and allocate resources to meet the private and public sector needs. At the outcome level, the programme sets out three main strategic objectives:

(i) strengthening Financial Markets Enabling Environment and Institutions through improved capital markets regulatory and legal environment and upgraded market infrastructure;

(ii) broadening Capital Markets Instruments and Market Participants through diversified capital markets product offerings, increasing number of securities supplied and broadened capital market participants; and,

(iii) strengthening Knowledge Management for Capital Market Issues in Africa through an expanded knowledge base and strengthened dissemination efforts.

To realize these strategic objectives, the programme targets to:

(i) improve capital markets regulatory and legal environment;

(ii) upgrade capital markets infrastructure;

(iii) diversify products;

(iv) broaden Africas investor base; and,

(v) increase knowledge on African capital markets. 

These interventions will not only contribute to building the requisite foundations of the domestic and regional African capital markets, but potentially have catalytic effect to crowd in investors to sectors with high development potential and financial returns. Currently, the programme's geographical coverage is West Africa, but through the funds from Sweden, as well as the support and flexibility of the existing donors, the CMDTF will extend its coverage towards the rest of the continent. The programme is demand-driven and has alreay verified demand beyond West Africa, including countries such as Rwanda, Ethiopia, Botswana and Zambia.

The main beneficiaries and stakeholders of the CMDTF include Stock Exchanges, Local/Regional Capital Markets Authorities, Institutional Investors and their regulators, Central Banks, Regional Economic Communities, Ministries of finance, Debt Management Offices, Ministries of Regional Integration, industry associations, and securities continental bodies.

Det övergripande målet för CMDTF är att främja etableringen av välfungerande kapitalmarknader i Afrika som effektivt mobiliserar och allokerar resurser för att möta den privata och offentliga sektorns finansieringsbehov. För att uppnå detta mål planerar CMDTF att:

i) Förbättra kapitalmarknadernas regelverk och juridiska miljö;

ii) Uppgradera kapitalmarknadernas infrastruktur;

iii) Diversifiera tillgängliga produkter;

iv) Bredda investerarbasen; och,

v) Öka kunskapen om de afrikanska kapitalmarknaderna.
